      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I understand wanting to avoid food waste, but moderation doesn't equate to safety when it comes to MAOIs. The concern with medicines like MAOIs is that they have a narrow therapeutic window, meaning there's not much room for error in consumption. That's why consuming even small amounts of certain foods with tyramine can still pose a risk. It's crucial to err on the side of caution and consult with your healthcare provider about suitable foods. There are plenty of safe, high-protein alternatives that won't compromise your medication's effectiveness or your health.",
