      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, you're on the right track. Fresh chicken, eggs, and plain, un-salted yogurt are safe choices that are also high in protein. It's true that plain yogurt doesn't have sufficient yeast fermentation to cause issues, but always check the label for added sugars or flavorings that might contain other ingredients to watch out for. Generally, fresh fruits, vegetables, lean meats, dairy products, and grains are good sources of protein for someone on MAOIs. Avoid, however, processed or aged foods and anything that might have been flavored or preservative-added due to the risks associated with your medication.",
